 "text": "Sound: a soft, hollow, woody pad, like a distant organ or clarinets: the gentle square-wave pads of early synth-pop.\n\nHow it's built: two squares (PULSE at 50 %), one an octave down, a little detuned; a soft Ladder filter; medium attack; Chorus and Reverb. Six voices.\n\nPlay: chords, held.\n\nTweak: the filter's CUTOFF, the octave square's level (mixer 2), the envelope.",
